"Additionally, if you want to do something that is invalid in the game, there "
"will be some message displayed on the statusbar. For example, if some cup is "
"empty and you still want to move from there, there will be a message like "
"<quote>Sorry, not enough stone to move</quote>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid "Basic Concept"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&mancala; currently has seven games included. These are: kalah, oware, "
"barbados_warri, bechi, dakon, sungka and chungka."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Before going to the detailed rules on each of them, I would like to tell the "
"basic rules of mancala games available. Discussing every game is beyond the "
"scope. I will only focus on the games that are included in this game."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All the two row games consist of a number of cups and a number of stones on "
"each cup. The number of cups may vary from game to game. A player has some "
"cups and a big cup which works as a storage. Stones moves from cup to cup, "
"but if once put to the storage never comes back. It will be yours for "
"lifetime."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid "We first define some criteria:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: index.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid "Minimum number of stones to sow"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The required number of stones in a cup for a valid move, varies from game to "
"game. For example: in kalah, it is one, but in bechi it is 2."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: index.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid "Number of stones remains after sow"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:128
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After the move is made, in some game the cup becomes empty, but in others it "
"requires to have a number of stones left. In kalah, cup becomes empty, in "
"bechi 1 stone is left."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: index.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid "Movement direction"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In some games, player moves clockwise and in some other games he moves "
"counter-clockwise. Conditional direction set is also allowed (in bechi)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: index.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid "<emphasis>Sowing</emphasis>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:140
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The movement from a player is called sowing. When a player's turn comes, he "
"has to select a cup, from where he is going to move/sow. Two different type "
"of sowing is allowed here:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:143
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Single Lap: In games like kalah. When a player selects a cup for move and "
"the cup has at least minimum number of stones to move, the number of stones "
"needed to remain on the cup are left and others are distributed (one stone "
"to each) to the following cups (in moving direction) or storages until stone "
"is finished. If the last stone is on storage a bonus turn is possible (if "
"allowed). A capture may be possible if the last stone is on player's cup "
"(Cross Capture, if allowed) or in opponent's cup (Count and series Capture)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:146
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Multiple Lap: If the last stone from the first sow, is on any cup which "
"makes the number of stones on the cup to make a valid move, then another "
"sowing is done. This process goes until the stone is on any cup, from where "
"move is invalid."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: index.docbook:152
#, no-c-format
msgid "<emphasis>Bonus Turn</emphasis>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:154
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In some game, bonus turn is allowed if the last stone is put on player's "
"storage. Example: kalah."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: index.docbook:158
#, no-c-format
msgid "<emphasis>Capture</emphasis>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:160
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Different types of capture is available in games. A precise description is "
"below:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:163
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Cross Capture: If the last stone is on a cup (at the player's side) that was "
"previously empty, then he can capture all the stones (if any) on the cup "
"across at his opponent's side. Example: kalah."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:166
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Count Capture: If the last stone is on a cup of the opponent which makes the "
"number of stone on the cup a specific number, then the stones on the cup can "
"be captured. Example: In oware, if the number is 2 or 3 count capture "
"possible."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:169
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Series Capture: If Count Capture is possible and the following or preceding "
"cups (depends on the game) on the opponent also contains the same number of "
"stones, then they are also captured until the law is broken. Examples: "
"oware, barbados warri, bechi."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:175
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this game, the first turn is of human (the player). The player's side is "
"the lower side. When the turn of a player comes, he needs to sow. If capture "
"is possible after sowing, then it is done. Or, if the player gets a bonus "
"turn (if allowed), he get another chance. After the end of player's turn, "
"computer gets it turn. The game continues this way. The goal of the game is "
"to maximize the number of stones in your storage. When all the stones are "
"finished game ends. The player who gets maximum stones is the winner."
msgstr ""

